  "code": {
    "framework": "react",
    "package": "@coinbase/cds-web",
    "component": "IconButton",
    "import": "import { IconButton } from '@coinbase/cds-web/buttons';",
    "alwaysEmit": [
      "size"
    ],
    "alwaysEmitWhy": "IconButton turns the deprecated compact on by default, so an IconButton without size renders at s while size is documented to default to l; emit size explicitly so the snippet keeps matching the variant when compact goes."
  },
  "notes": [
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "axes.variant",
      "message": "IconButton.tsx documents variant @default primary (L65-L69), but it destructures variant = 'secondary' (L113), and CDS's Code Connect file treats secondary as the default (IconButton.figma.ts L8). The Contract follows the code: the Base Component is Secondary."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "axes.size",
      "message": "IconButton turns the deprecated compact on by default (compact = true, IconButton.tsx L115), so resolvedSize = size ?? (compact ? 's' : defaultIconButtonSize) is 's' without a size (L144). The documented size @default l and defaultIconButtonSize = 'l' (L78-L84, L51) apply only with compact={false}. The Contract's default is s, what an IconButton without props renders, and code.alwaysEmit writes size in every snippet, as CDS's Code Connect does (IconButton.figma.ts L26-L28), so a snippet keeps its size when compact goes."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "axes.state",
      "message": "A loading IconButton is also disabled (Pressable.tsx L225-L227), and :disabled sets pointer-events: none (Interactable.tsx L66-L71), so in use a loading IconButton is never hovered, pressed or focused. Those 144 tuples render as the cascade draws them when the State is forced (the pressed background and child opacity of [data-loading='true'] win, Pressable.tsx L48-L54). They stay in the selection; the owner can omit them in To-preview."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "axes.state",
      "message": "Active takes the :active and [aria-pressed='true'] rules (Interactable.tsx L57-L64). Pressable's scaledDownCss also scales the IconButton to 0.98 on :active (Pressable.tsx L30-L38); a Component Set variant has no transform, so the Active variant is drawn at full size."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "paint[state=focus].IconButton.stroke",
      "message": "The focus ring is a 2px solid outline in bgPrimary, 2px outside the border box (outline-offset, Interactable.tsx L80-L85). The Contract draws it as a 2px outside stroke with no gap. A spread drop shadow could keep the gap, but bgPrimary has no EFFECT_COLOR scope in the foundations document, so an effect cannot bind it (validation rule 6)."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "layout.Spinner",
      "message": "While loading, IconButton renders the ProgressCircle in place of the Icon (IconButton.tsx L196-L216), at progressCircleSize ?? iconSizeValue (L202), the iconSize in px (L149): 16 at xs and s, 24 at m and l. So the Spinner sits in the flow where the Icon sat, at the Icon's size; it is not absolute as in Button. spinnerSize (L150) is computed but never used."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "paint.Spinner.opacity",
      "message": "Interactable and Pressable set opacity on the IconButton's direct children (> *: hovered, pressed and loading, Interactable.tsx L52-L54 and L61-L63, Pressable.tsx L48-L54). While loading, that child is the VisualizationContainer, a Box without a class around the Box that takes the className cds-IconButton-progressCircle (ProgressCircle.tsx L196-L219). The Contract has no layer for the container, so the Spinner takes its opacity: 0.82 while loading."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "layout.Arc.arc",
      "message": "The Arc is a still frame of an endless rotation. CDS spins the whole ProgressCircle forever (indeterminateProgressCircleCss, ProgressCircle.tsx L105-L115: 1000ms linear infinite) and starts its arc at 12 o'clock (rotate: -90, L137). The Contract draws that start: 270 degrees clockwise from 12 o'clock (an indeterminate progress of 0.75, L175, drawn as stroke-dashoffset 1 - 0.75 = 0.25, L132 and L140, of pathLength 1 and stroke-dasharray 1, L152-L153). Figma has no animation, so the Arc doesn't spin."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "layout.IconButton.strokeWeight",
      "message": "IconButton passes borderWidth = 0 (IconButton.tsx L121) with the variant's border colour, so no variant draws a border; stroke is none outside Focus. The variants' border tokens (button-<variant>-border) stay out of the closure."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "paint",
      "message": "IconButton paints with Button's token map: it imports transparentVariants and variants from cds-common's tokens/button (IconButton.tsx L2) and picks one by transparent (L165-L170). So it binds the button-<variant>[-transparent]-<background|color> component tokens and Button's Synthesized state tokens. cds-common has no IconButton token map, so the Foundations document carries no iconbutton tokens of its own."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "family",
      "message": "flush (a negative inline margin, IconButton.tsx L155-L163) changes how the IconButton sits in its parent, not how it draws, so it is not an axis. The padding, iconSize, progressCircleSize, borderRadius, background, color and borderColor props (L117-L132) override what the size and the variant set; the Contract draws the values IconButton picks. compact is the deprecated alias of size s (dropped from size)."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "properties.icon",
      "message": "name is required (IconButton.tsx L56-L57), so the Icon always shows unless loading, and the swap has no BOOLEAN. active (L63-L64) picks the active glyph of the same icon (L209); the icon source uses the inactive glyphs only."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "code",
      "message": "CDS's own Code Connect file (IconButton.figma.ts) maps three variants (L9-L13) and folds loading and disabled into one state property (L16-L24). The Contract follows IconButton.tsx: six variants, from ButtonBaseProps.ts, with Loading its own axis, as in Button."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "figma.page",
      "message": "IconButton gets a page of its own, Icon buttons, beside Button's Buttons: To-design's base slice records one page per family in its ledger and refuses a page of the same name that another family built (an unowned page)."
    }
  ],
